21
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:43,340
And so far, the groundwork that has been laid on the book of Revelation is maybe different than what you have heard, depending on what your background is,

22
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:47,600
and that is the book of Revelation is not a puzzle to be decoded, right?

23
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,680
It is not primarily about future events.

24
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:58,920
The book is a revealing of Jesus Christ to seven real churches in Asia Minor in the first century.

25
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,740
And so we've got to approach the book.

26
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:07,940
When we approach the book, we have to realize that it is literally a pulling back of the curtain.

27
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:10,640
That's why we're doing this kind of half open, half closed.

28
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:14,220
It's an optical illustration of what the book of Revelation is doing.

29
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:18,920
It's opening up the heavenly realms, the present realities of the heavenly realms,

30
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:21,620
for seven real churches in the first century.

31
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:25,960
It is written to encourage these churches who are struggling,

32
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:29,960
to challenge these churches who are in rebellion,

33
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,740
to wake up churches who are stagnant.

34
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:35,660
The letter can't mean to us what it did not mean to them.

35
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:39,420
So we've got to read it and try and best understand it in their context

36
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:43,000
before we jump to application for us.

37
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:49,880
And the primary message of the book of Revelation that encourages struggling churches,

38
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:53,660
challenges rebellious churches, and wakes up stagnant churches is all the same.

39
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:57,480
It is the risen Jesus reigning on his throne.

40
00:03:57,480 --> 00:04:01,140
That is the central theme of the book of Revelation.

41
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:07,540
And it is a unseen reality until John opens up the curtain for us and shows us it.

42
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:11,960
I love how Daryl Johnson in the book that I recommended summarizes the content of Revelation.

43
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:16,200
And if you want, you can throw up our graphic from the Ephesians series.

44
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,200
Because I think this is a helpful reminder.

45
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:20,220
You guys remember this from the Ephesians series if you were here?

46
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:24,720
All right, so this is helpful for the book of Revelation as well,

47
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:30,720
that we live in the present reality after the death, burial, and resurrection of Jesus.

48
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:34,400
Those of us who have placed our faith in Jesus, we find ourselves in the church,

49
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:38,700
in between the cross and the resurrection and new creation, God bringing heaven to earth.

50
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:42,500
This is the prayer that may your kingdom come and your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

51
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:46,720
We live in between these two moments where the kingdom of God has been inaugurated

52
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,840
but not yet consummated.

53
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:52,780
And you see how we kind of cut the curtain there open to the heavenly spaces.

54
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:55,540
That's what the gospel, or that's what the book of Revelation is doing.

55
00:04:55,540 --> 00:05:01,580
It's opening up to the church what the present realities of heaven are.

56
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:04,540
And again, I love how Daryl Johnson summarizes it.

57
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:05,160
He says this,

58
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:11,500
Revelation sets the present realities in light of the unseen realities of the future.

59
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:16,660
And it sets the present realities in light of the unseen realities of the present.

60
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:24,780
And so what he's saying here is, Revelation is showing the church what heaven is like right now.

61
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:30,640
As we speak, as we gather together, there is heavenly worship happening in the throne room right now.

62
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:32,840
Next week, we're going to get a picture of what that looks like.

63
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,320
John's pulling back the curtain.

64
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:38,100
He's showing us what the heavenly places look like right now.

65
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:50,240
So that we know, even when the empires of this world look powerful, even when things get hard, even when it looks like we are not victorious, we can be reminded of what is happening behind the curtain.

66
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:53,060
That Jesus is victorious, whether we see it or not.

67
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:56,680
And there's a future reality where we will see it that we are waiting for.

68
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:04,320
So this is the context for the book of Revelation, that we are in this already not yet space.

69
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:14,340
And the book of Revelation opens up the curtain so that we can see what is presently happening in the spiritual heavenly places and what will happen in the future.

70
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:18,940
And I love how Kent summarized his goal of the content last week.

71
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:23,160
He said, the goal of this whole series is not to better understand what Revelation means.

72
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:28,000
The goal is to understand what Revelation is calling us to do.

73
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,840
Or how is the book of Revelation inviting us to live?

74
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:36,020
The goal should not be just to understand what these images mean.

75
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:40,400
The goal should be to understand what these images have to do with how we live in this present world.

76
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:49,640
And unfortunately, if I've got to be honest, pastorally, the book of Revelation is probably one of the books that many Christians love to study the most.

77
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:59,400
And the thing that scares me is the way in which they study it is we found a way to study this book in such a way that it doesn't have any practical implications on our life whatsoever.

78
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:07,840
And so I think there's this weird deception that the enemy is using where Christians feel good because they love to study the Bible.

79
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:11,940
But they're only studying the book in a way that doesn't impact their everyday lives.

80
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:17,720
And so what we want to do is we want to try and study this book in such a way that it challenges the way that we live.

81
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:21,500
That it encourages us in the midst of our suffering and our difficulty.

82
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:27,480
That this message isn't just about decoding the future, but it's about our present reality right now.

83
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:36,900
And hopefully today's message will get us one step further in this idea of how this book is calling us to live.

84
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:42,000
And we're going to do a big overview of chapters two and three in the seven messages to the seven churches.

85
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,420
Does that sound good to you all?

86
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:45,720
Okay, let's do it.

87
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,960
Let's pray and get started.

88
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,840
We already started.

89
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:50,880
That was, I preached a little bit there.

90
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,560
It was a little preaching.

91
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:52,100
All right, let's pray.

92
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,580
Father, we love you.

93
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:58,920
We thank you that you have given us a peek behind the curtain.

94
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:10,400
That you have allowed us to see present spiritual realities that, if I'm honest, don't always feel like they're true.

95
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:25,780
That in a world marred and broken by sin, in a world full of suffering and discouragement and difficulty, God, it can often feel as if the Christian life is one of defeat and sorrow and pain.

96
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:29,980
And yet you have opened up the curtain for us.

97
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:43,680
You have shown us that the Christian life is worth persevering because there is present victory in heaven and future victory awaiting those of us who remain faithful to the lamb as though he is slain.

98
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:48,240
And so, Holy Spirit, have your way in this gathering today.

99
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:51,880
Speak to us through these messages to these real churches.

100
00:08:51,880 --> 00:09:03,840
God, these are real people with real lives and real cultural moments who really were suffering, who really were discouraged, who really were stagnant or missing the mark for what it means for them to be Christians.

101
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,680
And those lives translate to our lives today.

102
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:09,720
God, many of us in the room are suffering or persecuted or struggling.

103
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,340
Many of us are stagnant.

104
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:12,140
We need to wake up.

105
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:13,660
Many of us are in rebellion.

106
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:14,460
We need to repent.

107
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:22,180
God, these messages to these churches are not just an ancient text to be studied.

108
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:26,300
It is your living and active word to pierce our hearts.

109
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:29,940
God, do that through your word by the power of your Holy Spirit.

110
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,580
In Jesus' name I pray.

111
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:32,560
Amen.

112
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:38,980
All right, so we will read some in Revelation 1, 2, and 3.

113
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:42,460
But for the most part, we're going to be doing some high-level, big-picture overviews.

114
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:54,240
And what I want to ask today is, if you'll be honest with me, have you ever sat through the beginning of one of our services only to realize halfway through announcements that you have no clue what the person on stage said?

115
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,900
All right.

116
00:09:55,900 --> 00:10:00,720
I was hoping you would say yes, because if you didn't, I was going to call your bluff.

117
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:11,900
I actually have to pay for April, our office manager's therapy, because every week she says, you'll never believe somebody came up to me and said, when did we announce that we were doing this thing?

118
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:18,260
And she's in charge of announcements, and she's like, this day, this day, in this newsletter, through this text message, and on this.

119
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:21,300
So, like, we're speaking, right?

120
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:22,200
We are announcing.

121
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,040
We are declaring.

122
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:25,100
We are proclaiming these messages.

123
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:32,540
But oftentimes, even though we're here, we're present, we're in the room, there's someone at center stage with a microphone.

124
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:34,200
Your ears work.

125
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,500
Their voice works.

126
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:41,120
You hear every word coming out of their mouth, but the reality is you weren't really listening.

127
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:44,940
And this is not me condemning you for not listening to announcements.

128
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:46,720
It's just an illustration.

129
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:51,080
If April was up here, she would be condemning you for not listening to announcements.

130
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:53,580
And she might have a point.

131
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:56,140
But right now, I'm just using this as an illustration, okay?

132
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:57,700
I just want to get, okay.

133
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:00,640
I don't want you to get convicted over the wrong thing, all right?

134
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:02,320
We're going to get to the conviction part later.

135
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,380
This is just an illustration.

136
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:03,760
All right.

137
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:12,420
Because there is a difference between hearing sounds and giving someone your attention, right?

138
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:23,260
We can hear people make words and declarations with their mouth, and we cannot process those things because we're not giving them our full attention.

139
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:35,760
And in Revelation 2 and 3, Jesus repeats the phrase seven times, he who has ears to hear, listen to what the Spirit says to the churches.

140
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:47,380
And I'm afraid what happens to these churches and what often happens to us is the same thing that happens to you during announcements, and that is Jesus is speaking to his churches.

141
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:54,560
He is speaking to you, and maybe you hear his voice, but the question is, are you giving his voice your attention?

142
00:11:54,560 --> 00:12:02,320
Are you listening to what he is saying and turning and translating that listening into obeying?

143
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,980
The issue is not whether or not Jesus is speaking.

144
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:06,900
He is.

145
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:10,220
And John reveals that very clearly to us.

146
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:13,420
The issue is whether or not we are listening.

147
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,840
Or to take it a step further, whether or not we are giving him our undivided attention.

148
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:25,100
And this is, Revelation is pulling back the curtain and saying there's two present realities at work here.

149
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,520
Which one are you giving your undivided attention to?

150
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:32,060
And how is that impacting your life?

151
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:38,100
So with the rest of our time, again, I want to do a flyover of these two chapters so that we can better understand

152
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:42,980
who is Jesus to his churches in Revelation 2 and 3.

153
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:45,020
Who are the churches?

154
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:47,240
How are they receiving this message?

155
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:55,700
And what do these messages have to say about how we, in the 21st century, can function as the church in this present age,

156
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:58,460
where we're in between the kingdom being inaugurated and consummated,

157
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:01,900
where we're suffering, we're discouraged, we're hurting, we're persecuted.

158
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:07,300
How do we interact with the king who is sitting on the throne presently today?

159
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:09,040
So that's the plan for the rest of our time.

160
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:14,580
So first I want to look at who is Jesus to these churches.

161
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:17,080
In Revelation, we're going to start in chapter 1.

162
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:21,600
Starting in verse 10, it says this,

163
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:28,040
I, John, was in the Spirit on the Lord's Day, and I heard a loud voice behind me like a trumpet saying,

164
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:33,600
Write on a scroll what you see and send it to the seven churches.

165
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:38,780
Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea.

166
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:43,840
And then I turned to see whose voice it was that spoke to me.

167
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:48,840
And when I turned, I saw, he saw seven golden lampstands,

168
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:54,720
and among the lampstands was one like the Son of Man dressed in a robe

169
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:57,800
with a golden sash wrapped around his chest.

170
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:01,500
And we skipped to verse 20, and we read,

171
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:07,080
The mystery of the seven stars you saw in my right hand

172
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:10,260
and of the seven golden lampstands is this.

173
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:13,700
The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches,

174
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:18,220
and the seven lampstands are the seven churches.

175
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:23,040
And so right from the outset, before we even get to the messages

176
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,980
that is going to be given to the seven churches,

177
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:28,980
the picture that we see of Jesus is one like a Son of Man

178
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:33,520
who is walking among his churches.

179
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:37,920
In verse 13, I don't want us to miss this.

180
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,820
This is so beautiful.

181
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:39,680
It's so powerful.

182
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:43,960
And among the lampstands, it could be translated,

183
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:48,260
in the middle of the lampstands was one like the Son of Man dressed in a robe.

184
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:51,600
And then verse 20 tells us very clearly, what are the seven lampstands?

185
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,720
They are the seven churches.

186
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:57,000
What John wants us to know before we ever get a message from Jesus

187
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:00,240
is that this Jesus walks among his churches.

188
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:03,620
The same Jesus who is risen and reigning and sitting on a throne

189
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:06,240
is present and active among his churches.

190
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:10,320
He doesn't just rule and reign from a throne far away,

191
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:14,400
but he is present and active in the middle of his churches.

192
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:18,040
Before Jesus says anything to his churches,

193
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,240
we need to know that who he is,

194
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:24,040
that he is not just simply giving us an encouraging word from a wise teacher,

195
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:28,820
that he is the Son of Man, risen from the dead, reigning and present.

196
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:32,840
He is already on the throne.

197
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:35,020
Caesar may appear powerful.

198
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:37,880
The Romans may treat him like God.

199
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:41,880
The empire may appear to rule, but Jesus alone is the true authority.

200
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:44,000
This is the pulling back of the curtain.

201
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,160
This is the apocalypse.

202
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,340
This is the revelation.

203
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:49,960
John is setting the visible present reality

204
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,500
in light of the unseen realities of the present.

205
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:57,620
And importantly, for struggling churches that exist in the Roman Empire,

206
00:15:57,620 --> 00:15:59,920
Jesus isn't just reigning from heaven.

207
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:03,300
He is present in the middle of his churches.

208
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:10,260
Each message that he gives is extremely, extremely contextual.

209
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:13,020
Seven times we read the phrase,

210
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:15,680
I know from Jesus to these seven churches.

211
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:17,640
I know your works.

212
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,740
I know your suffering.

213
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:21,640
I know your compromise.

214
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:23,920
I know your weakness.

215
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:26,240
Jesus is among his churches.

216
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,960
He is not sitting far away and distant.

217
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:32,580
He is present and he knows what's going on in our seven churches.

218
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:33,760
He knows where we're faithful.

219
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,180
He knows where we aren't.

220
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:39,500
The risen and reigning king of the universe is present.

221
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:44,980
He sees what no one else does and he knows what is true of us

