00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:13,180
Here's where I need you to wake up, repent, open your eyes, figure some stuff out, right?

328
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:14,220
Minus two churches.

329
00:23:14,220 --> 00:23:21,000
So two churches don't get any encouragement, and two churches don't get any consequences.

330
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,040
It's just like, you guys are doing great.

331
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:30,100
And then at the end, he will offer these, again, contextualized announcements of blessings and cursings.

332
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:35,760
If you are faithful, if you wake up, if you repent, if you heed my words,

333
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:42,980
if you listen, right, not just hear, but if you listen to my words, you will conquer and you will receive blessing.

334
00:23:42,980 --> 00:23:45,680
But if you do not, there's threats, right?

335
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,100
I will take the lampstand away.

336
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:49,200
You will lose your influence and your power, right?

337
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:52,040
There's blessings and cursings.

338
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:56,300
And to each church, the message starts.

339
00:23:56,300 --> 00:24:10,660
And I want to focus on this word church so that we make sure we understand how we are to function in relationship to the risen and reigning king who walks among his churches.

340
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:19,220
And this is a word that we use all the time, and it's so common to us that we do not, we miss the cultural impact that it would have had on the first century.

341
00:24:19,560 --> 00:24:28,080
The Greek word ekklesia, it's translated church, it's so common to us, it's just what we think of about a gathering of believers in a building like this.

342
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:31,720
But to them, it had massive cultural implications.

343
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:35,340
Ekklesia in the first century was not primarily a religious word.

344
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:37,740
It was a secular word.

345
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:47,680
One scholar translates it this way, that the word ekklesia literally in the first century Greek meant a gathering of citizens to conduct civic business.

346
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:58,720
This is a group of people who were coming together to make decisions for the empire, to make decisions for their township, to do civic duty.

347
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:06,720
And John and the apostles and Jesus intentionally co-opt this word and use it for the gathering of believers.

348
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:20,400
And I think what we should get here is that when John gives us a peek behind the curtain, he emphasizes that the church in the New Testament, much like Israel in the Old Testament, is God's sovereign nation on earth.

349
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:32,560
Jews and Gentiles, male and female, slave and free, we are all gathered together as one new people, citizens of one new kingdom, under the reign and rule of Jesus.

350
00:25:32,560 --> 00:25:36,840
This is a politically charged word aimed at our primary allegiance.

351
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:42,280
No longer boundaried by one geographic location, but spread across the world.

352
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:51,240
Even the choice to use the word church is saying something about how we should function to our risen and reigning king.

353
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:53,860
Saying it looks like Rome is in power.

354
00:25:53,860 --> 00:25:57,380
It looks like Rome is persecuting, but I am on the throne.

355
00:25:57,380 --> 00:26:00,680
Are you a citizen of Rome or are you a citizen of the kingdom?

356
00:26:01,320 --> 00:26:06,100
Are you gathered together to do kingdom business or are you gathered together to do Roman business?

357
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:18,040
And this is going to lead into some of the correcting messages to some of the churches because some of the churches are more concerned with their success and their power and their influence in Rome than they are in the kingdom of the agenda of God's kingdom moving forward.

358
00:26:19,300 --> 00:26:21,860
Do we understand the influence, the implications here?

359
00:26:21,860 --> 00:26:28,480
So he says to the church, and then every message starts with a thus says.

360
00:26:29,140 --> 00:26:39,540
So on top of it being a message to the church, the rest of the form also tells us something about how we should interact with Jesus, the risen, reigning king.

361
00:26:40,420 --> 00:26:59,340
Many scholars point out that the form, thus says, title, encouragement, blessing, cursing, all of that, the pattern we just talked about, that it actually overarching looks like two types, two genres of literature that the audience would have been familiar with.

362
00:26:59,340 --> 00:26:59,900
Okay.

363
00:26:59,900 --> 00:27:03,520
The first genre is Old Testament prophetic oracles.

364
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:07,960
So if you go back, you read Ezekiel, you read Isaiah, you read Hosea.

365
00:27:08,140 --> 00:27:18,340
Like when the prophet would speak to God's people on behalf of God, he would say things like, thus says Yahweh, here's where you're doing good.

366
00:27:18,340 --> 00:27:19,880
Here's where you're doing bad.

367
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:23,040
Here's what you need to do to repent, to change your ways.

368
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:25,940
And if you repent, here's the blessing that God will give.

369
00:27:25,940 --> 00:27:28,260
If you do not repent, here's what will happen.

370
00:27:28,260 --> 00:27:29,040
Right?

371
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:31,020
That's the pattern that we see in Revelation.

372
00:27:31,020 --> 00:27:37,200
This is a familiar pattern that the Jews specifically would have been very familiar with.

373
00:27:38,140 --> 00:27:47,360
They would have heard, okay, God is, this is Yahweh speaking to us, like a, this is John speaking like a prophet of Yahweh to the church.

374
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:47,760
Okay?

375
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:55,500
But the other thing that many scholars point out is that it also follows some very similar patterns to first century imperial edicts.

376
00:27:55,980 --> 00:28:12,900
So again, think about Ezekiel, so Rome would gather a township of people together for civic duty, civic business, and somebody would come and read an imperial edict from the Roman Empire, and the imperial edict would say, thus says the governor of such and such.

377
00:28:13,940 --> 00:28:16,980
You guys are a great Roman city doing these things.

378
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:21,680
You're also doing these things that we need you to stop doing in order to be good Roman citizens.

379
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:25,180
And if you don't, we'll do empire things to you.

380
00:28:25,180 --> 00:28:26,780
Okay?

381
00:28:26,780 --> 00:28:38,600
So what I want to say is that the term, the use of ekklesia in the form of the letters is communicating two really clear things to the first century that we miss when we just read it in English.

382
00:28:38,940 --> 00:28:43,360
That we miss when we just try and read it as if it's a message to us and not to these first century churches.

383
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:51,080
And that is that good Jewish Christians would have understood that John was speaking to them as a prophet on behalf of Yahweh.

384
00:28:51,080 --> 00:28:59,160
And good Gentile Christians would have heard, wow, this sounds a lot like how our governor talks to us when he gathers us together for civic business.

385
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:05,200
They would have heard a king inviting them to be faithful and productive citizens.

386
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:13,000
And the point that I want to make is that Revelation is extending, in my opinion, it's extending both of these invitations as a package deal.

387
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:20,080
The church is both worshipers summoned before a holy God and citizens summoned before a reigning king.

388
00:29:20,080 --> 00:29:21,420
The two cannot be separated.

389
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:26,480
And oftentimes in American Christianity, we want to separate these two things.

390
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:29,180
We just want to be worshipers before a holy God.

391
00:29:29,180 --> 00:29:39,100
And then we want to be American citizens that may or may not have implications on the kingdom of God in our everyday lives.

392
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:44,580
And so I just want to make sure we don't lose sight of what's happening in the first century.

393
00:29:44,580 --> 00:29:47,040
And two cannot be separated.

394
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:53,140
Revelation 2 and 3 reminds us that we are citizens of another kingdom and that our king requires ultimate allegiance.

