439
00:32:46,740 --> 00:32:50,760
There's all of this text about live for the flourishing of the people that you live among.

440
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:54,020
It's not that we don't care about the success of America.

441
00:32:54,020 --> 00:33:02,060
It's just that when those two things come at odds, our primary allegiance is to the kingdom of Jesus.

442
00:33:02,060 --> 00:33:07,520
And I fear that many of us have been discipled to be Americans first, Christians second.

443
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:10,380
The book is regularly going to confront us with this reality.

444
00:33:10,380 --> 00:33:16,000
The form of the message given to the seven churches is Jesus calling us to give our primary allegiance to him.

445
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,440
All right, that's enough.

446
00:33:17,440 --> 00:33:18,440
Soapbox is done.

447
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:19,420
Can we take another deep breath?

448
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:30,940
All right, and seriously, I know that this is not the majority message that's being given from pulpits

449
00:33:30,940 --> 00:33:34,980
across the country on our 250th anniversary.

450
00:33:34,980 --> 00:33:39,580
And so what I want you to do is if you have problems with what I'm saying

451
00:33:39,580 --> 00:33:44,380
and you think that it's not reflected in the words of Jesus, in the message of Scripture,

452
00:33:44,780 --> 00:33:48,700
please don't like just leave the church out the back door and say,

453
00:33:48,700 --> 00:33:49,480
that guy's crazy.

454
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:53,100
I'm going to go find a church that celebrates, that's patriotic.

455
00:33:53,100 --> 00:33:54,420
Please send me an email.

456
00:33:54,420 --> 00:33:58,320
Please sit down and have coffee with me because I could be wrong.

457
00:33:58,320 --> 00:34:01,240
You could be wrong.

458
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:03,980
The reality is we're probably both a little bit wrong.

459
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:11,020
And the kingdom of God is far too important for us to separate over secondary issues.

460
00:34:11,020 --> 00:34:12,340
Okay, my soapbox is done.

461
00:34:12,340 --> 00:34:12,880
We've got to move on.

462
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:16,000
All right.

463
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:19,180
Now, does anybody wonder why there's seven churches?

464
00:34:19,180 --> 00:34:20,160
Why not eight?

465
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:20,860
Why not 11?

466
00:34:20,860 --> 00:34:21,760
Why not four?

467
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,240
Right?

468
00:34:23,240 --> 00:34:26,000
And why these seven churches particularly?

469
00:34:27,140 --> 00:34:32,720
Well, seven is a, the Jews would have immediately heard that this is a number of completeness.

470
00:34:32,720 --> 00:34:34,580
This is a symbolic number.

471
00:34:34,580 --> 00:34:39,720
Many scholars believe Jesus wrote to these seven churches because they represent the overarching

472
00:34:39,720 --> 00:34:43,580
challenges that all churches throughout all history will face.

473
00:34:43,580 --> 00:34:48,120
Or at least every church can be encouraged or rebuked by one of these messages.

474
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:54,140
So the theory is that all seven of these messages, the way Jesus speaks to these seven churches

475
00:34:54,140 --> 00:34:57,780
is a message that all the churches throughout history will need.

476
00:34:57,780 --> 00:35:06,480
So that the church in, the underground church in China can read through Revelation 2 and 3

477
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:09,620
and they can get something for where they're at in their current cultural moment.

478
00:35:09,620 --> 00:35:14,940
That the Revelation 2 and 3 speaks to the underground church in China and to the church in America

479
00:35:14,940 --> 00:35:18,140
and South Africa and name your country, right?

480
00:35:18,140 --> 00:35:22,720
The reality is we think that Jesus gave these churches, these messages because the overarching,

481
00:35:23,260 --> 00:35:26,860
if you just read all of them, you can get something for every church in all time.

482
00:35:26,860 --> 00:35:31,200
And again, we don't have time to cover the specifics of all seven churches.

483
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:36,820
But as I was studying and praying and considering what all of these messages say,

484
00:35:36,820 --> 00:35:46,100
I saw three competing voices that I think show up, if I were to give categories that fit into all seven,

485
00:35:46,100 --> 00:35:54,680
there's three voices that are in all seven churches distracting the church from listening to the voice of Jesus.

486
00:35:54,680 --> 00:36:03,480
Remember seven times Jesus says, hear, he who has ears to hear, listen to what the Spirit is saying.

487
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:09,780
There are voices that are at work in all seven churches that are trying to distract the church from hearing the voice of God,

488
00:36:09,780 --> 00:36:12,520
distract the church from paying attention to the voice of God,

489
00:36:12,520 --> 00:36:17,280
distract the church from giving their total allegiance to the voice of Jesus.

490
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:22,020
Every church Jesus writes to is facing unique circumstances and challenges.

491
00:36:22,020 --> 00:36:28,560
But underneath every message is the same question, whose voice will shape God's people?

492
00:36:28,560 --> 00:36:32,020
Whose voice will the church listen to?

493
00:36:32,680 --> 00:36:37,960
And the body of each message confronts the churches with the voices that are in competition for their attention.

494
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:47,760
And the invitation again at the end of each message is he who has ears, listen to the Lamb who is risen and reigning and you will conquer.

495
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:50,980
That's the message overly seven times.

496
00:36:50,980 --> 00:36:54,720
You will conquer to the one who has ears, listen and you will conquer.

497
00:36:54,720 --> 00:36:55,540
You will overcome.

498
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:00,060
So, three voices.

499
00:37:00,060 --> 00:37:02,380
Number one, we're doing all right.

500
00:37:02,380 --> 00:37:02,940
We'll figure it out.

501
00:37:02,940 --> 00:37:03,260
All right.

502
00:37:03,260 --> 00:37:04,400
Deception.

503
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:10,220
Both Pergamum and Thyatira were threatened by the voices of deception.

504
00:37:10,220 --> 00:37:16,280
Whether it be false teachers who are teaching them things in the Scriptures that aren't true,

505
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:22,320
that are leading them astray by manipulating the Scriptures to make it say what they want it to say for their own profit,

506
00:37:22,700 --> 00:37:29,760
or by culture, promising them that they can follow Jesus and simultaneously enjoy the value system of the culture around them.

507
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:37,680
These are voices of distraction that are seeking to lead the church astray from listening to the voice of Jesus.

508
00:37:37,680 --> 00:37:43,760
False teachers distorting biblical truth, telling Christians what they want to hear for their own profit or reputation.

509
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:47,820
And if you follow Christian leaders that have massive social media platforms today,

510
00:37:47,820 --> 00:37:51,860
I will tell you that this distraction, this deception still exists.

511
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:56,300
Or you can find, you can find a religious teacher who will tell you what you want to hear.

512
00:37:56,300 --> 00:38:01,860
And oftentimes, if we step back and figure out why their platforms are so big,

513
00:38:01,860 --> 00:38:07,680
many times it's because they get a, they make profit by telling you what you want to hear.

514
00:38:07,680 --> 00:38:10,040
This happens today in the church.

515
00:38:10,040 --> 00:38:17,540
Cultural systems invite Christians to keep their Christianity private while publicly conforming to the practices of secular culture.

516
00:38:17,540 --> 00:38:20,620
Still happens today.

517
00:38:21,460 --> 00:38:27,060
To both of these voices of deception, the invitation from Jesus is to repent.

518
00:38:27,060 --> 00:38:31,060
He gives different invitations to different voices.

519
00:38:31,060 --> 00:38:32,940
The voice to deception is repent.

520
00:38:32,940 --> 00:38:34,280
You're being led astray.

521
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:35,980
You have bad ideas.

522
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,000
Change your mind.

523
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,140
Believe what is true.

524
00:38:38,140 --> 00:38:40,080
Don't believe the lie.

525
00:38:40,080 --> 00:38:43,180
The second voice is that of distraction.

526
00:38:43,180 --> 00:38:48,820
Ephesus, Sardis, and Laodicea are all distracted from the voice of Jesus by lesser things.

527
00:38:49,140 --> 00:38:52,660
In Ephesus, it's doctrinal purity without loving their neighbors.

528
00:38:52,660 --> 00:38:59,300
Literally says, you can spot a false teacher from a mile away, but you do not have love in your heart.

529
00:39:01,460 --> 00:39:04,740
Does that exist in the American church today?

530
00:39:04,740 --> 00:39:13,620
Are there people that are obsessed with, with theology and with getting doctrine right who don't look anything like Jesus in the way that they behave or treat their neighbor?

531
00:39:15,220 --> 00:39:17,400
Ministry busyness is Sardis' issue.

532
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:19,760
They're, they're full of activity.

533
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:21,420
The church is doing all kinds of stuff.

534
00:39:21,420 --> 00:39:23,400
But Jesus says, your works are incomplete.

535
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:26,020
You're just busy for busyness sake.

536
00:39:26,020 --> 00:39:32,320
You're just doing things that aren't providing kingdom value, but you're feeling good about what you're doing because you're staying busy.

537
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:35,460
You're distracted from real kingdom work with ministry busyness.

538
00:39:35,580 --> 00:39:36,920
Does this happen today in the church?

539
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:38,160
Does this happen in our church?

540
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:46,080
Laodicea, you're distracted by worldly wealth and success without kingdom impact.

541
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:53,420
You care way more about what your bank accounts look like, about what your outfits look like than you do the kingdom of God.

542
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:58,260
And these distractions still threaten individuals and churches to this day.

543
00:39:58,260 --> 00:40:01,380
Many Christians love theology, but not their neighbors.

544
00:40:01,380 --> 00:40:04,840
We're busy running programs as churches that aren't building the kingdom.

545
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:09,720
We care more about comfort and success than we do what Jesus is calling us to.

546
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:13,800
And the voice of distraction is more subtle than false teaching.

547
00:40:13,800 --> 00:40:14,940
It happens slower.

548
00:40:14,940 --> 00:40:16,700
It happens over time.

549
00:40:16,700 --> 00:40:23,020
You add a program here, you add a program there, you upgrade your car, you do this, you do that.

550
00:40:23,020 --> 00:40:24,380
It happens slowly over time.

551
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:29,120
And before you know it, your primary affection is on the distraction rather than Jesus.

552
00:40:29,120 --> 00:40:35,380
And the message that Jesus gives to the churches that are distracted is not repent, it's wake up.

553
00:40:35,380 --> 00:40:37,240
Be alert.

554
00:40:37,240 --> 00:40:39,160
You're losing focus.

555
00:40:39,160 --> 00:40:40,660
Wake up.

556
00:40:40,660 --> 00:40:42,060
See what you're doing.

557
00:40:42,060 --> 00:40:42,980
You're being distracted.

558
00:40:42,980 --> 00:40:46,120
You're being lulled to sleep by busyness and by distraction.

559
00:40:46,120 --> 00:40:46,960
Wake up.

560
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:49,940
He who has ears to hear, listen.

561
00:40:51,140 --> 00:40:53,980
The last voice is that of discouragement.

562
00:40:53,980 --> 00:40:59,960
Both Smyrna and Philadelphia were enduring persecution faithfully.

563
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:04,980
It's no accident that, remember I said there's two churches that didn't receive any correction?

564
00:41:06,020 --> 00:41:10,200
It's the two churches that were suffering that didn't receive any correction.

565
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:15,100
And my hunch is that they're not perfect churches, but they're enduring suffering faithfully.

566
00:41:15,100 --> 00:41:19,940
And so Jesus isn't going to come to them when they're down and be like, nitpick a few things over here.

567
00:41:19,940 --> 00:41:20,920
Let me tell you what you're doing wrong.

568
00:41:20,980 --> 00:41:23,520
No, he comes to them with encouragement because they're suffering.

569
00:41:23,520 --> 00:41:30,700
But he warns them that this voice of discouragement can lead them astray.

570
00:41:30,700 --> 00:41:37,940
That if they keep on being discouraged, they might lose sight of the fact that Jesus died and has risen.

571
00:41:38,560 --> 00:41:41,900
That the one on the throne looks like a slain lamb.

572
00:41:41,900 --> 00:41:48,040
That oftentimes our victory, our conquering in Jesus can look like suffering.

573
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:55,200
But it's when we're in the midst of the suffering that we can take our eyes off of Jesus and just avoid suffering rather than to lead on to Jesus.

574
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:58,400
The message to these churches is to hold on.

575
00:41:58,400 --> 00:42:00,560
Cling to me, Jesus says.

576
00:42:00,560 --> 00:42:04,300
It's not wake up.

577
00:42:04,300 --> 00:42:05,080
It's not repent.

578
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:06,020
It's hold on.

579
00:42:06,020 --> 00:42:09,760
Cling to me in the midst of your suffering.

580
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:18,560
And because of all the things, all of the wonderful, beautiful, thankful things we said about our country,

581
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:23,000
the church in America, for pretty much all situations,

582
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:25,560
we're not being persecuted for being Christians in America.

583
00:42:25,560 --> 00:42:28,820
But just imagine with me,

584
00:42:28,820 --> 00:42:32,460
our brothers and sisters in places all over the country,

585
00:42:32,460 --> 00:42:35,240
all over the world where it's illegal to be Christians.

586
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:38,720
Imagine with me them reading the message to Sardis.

587
00:42:38,720 --> 00:42:44,700
And thinking about their brothers and sisters from 2,000 years ago

588
00:42:44,700 --> 00:42:47,060
who faithfully endured suffering and conquered.

589
00:42:47,060 --> 00:42:51,220
Imagine them reading,

590
00:42:52,020 --> 00:42:53,820
thus says the first and the last,

591
00:42:53,820 --> 00:42:55,820
the one who was dead and came to life again.

592
00:42:55,820 --> 00:42:56,900
I know your affliction.

593
00:42:56,900 --> 00:42:58,900
I know your poverty.

594
00:42:58,900 --> 00:43:01,940
But you are rich.

595
00:43:01,940 --> 00:43:10,660
Far more rich than anyone in your country who has all of the material worldly success.

596
00:43:10,660 --> 00:43:14,480
Let me pull back the curtain for you and show you what is the true meaning of this life.

597
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:17,220
You, persecuted church, you are rich.

598
00:43:20,420 --> 00:43:20,960
He says,

599
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:23,080
don't be afraid of what you are about to suffer.

600
00:43:23,080 --> 00:43:25,400
Look, the devil is going to throw some of you into prison.

601
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,620
Again, he's reminding them,

602
00:43:26,620 --> 00:43:28,620
your struggle is not against flesh and blood.

603
00:43:28,620 --> 00:43:32,940
The people that are throwing you in prison are not your enemies.

604
00:43:32,940 --> 00:43:35,360
Satan is your enemy.

605
00:43:35,360 --> 00:43:39,840
This is why people like Paul get thrown into prison

606
00:43:39,840 --> 00:43:43,640
and witness to the people keeping the jail

607
00:43:43,640 --> 00:43:45,400
because he knows that guy's not my enemy.

608
00:43:46,360 --> 00:43:48,320
That person on the other political aisle,

609
00:43:48,320 --> 00:43:49,340
that person with that opinion,

610
00:43:49,340 --> 00:43:50,100
they're not my enemy.

611
00:43:50,100 --> 00:43:52,440
They're a neighbor to be loved.

612
00:43:52,440 --> 00:43:54,200
Satan is the real enemy.

613
00:43:54,200 --> 00:43:58,080
And I love what he says.

614
00:43:58,080 --> 00:44:01,320
You will experience affliction for 10 days.

615
00:44:02,320 --> 00:44:04,640
I don't think he literally means 10 days.

616
00:44:04,640 --> 00:44:08,560
I think what he's saying is the devil is on a leash.

617
00:44:08,560 --> 00:44:10,500
He can only do so much.

618
00:44:10,500 --> 00:44:11,600
Look who's on the throne.

619
00:44:11,600 --> 00:44:13,800
Peel back the curtain.

620
00:44:13,800 --> 00:44:15,060
I have conquered.

621
00:44:15,060 --> 00:44:16,740
I am reigning.

622
00:44:16,740 --> 00:44:19,340
You might suffer temporarily right now,

623
00:44:19,340 --> 00:44:21,400
but it is a short-term suffering.

624
00:44:21,400 --> 00:44:23,040
And if you keep your eyes on me,

625
00:44:23,040 --> 00:44:24,040
if you cling to me,

626
00:44:24,040 --> 00:44:25,140
if you hold tight to me,

627
00:44:25,140 --> 00:44:26,200
you will conquer.

628
00:44:26,980 --> 00:44:28,340
He who has ears,

629
00:44:28,340 --> 00:44:29,960
listen.

630
00:44:29,960 --> 00:44:34,460
And as a church in America,

631
00:44:34,460 --> 00:44:36,160
we might not be persecuted for our faith,

632
00:44:36,160 --> 00:44:38,380
but many of us as individuals in the room are suffering

633
00:44:38,380 --> 00:44:40,820
through no fault of our own.

634
00:44:40,820 --> 00:44:42,940
Whether it's spiritual attack

635
00:44:42,940 --> 00:44:44,600
or you're just facing the consequences

636
00:44:44,600 --> 00:44:45,980
of living in a broken world,

637
00:44:45,980 --> 00:44:49,960
I think the same message from Jesus applies to you today.

638
00:44:49,960 --> 00:44:50,700
Hold on.

639
00:44:50,700 --> 00:44:53,140
Cling to me.

640
00:44:54,580 --> 00:44:55,760
And I got to be honest with you,

641
00:44:55,760 --> 00:44:56,100
I'm,

642
00:44:56,100 --> 00:44:56,480
I'm.

643
00:44:56,480 --> 00:45:02,820
Thanks.

644
00:45:02,820 --> 00:45:05,340
My family's in a season

645
00:45:05,340 --> 00:45:06,940
where we're going through some suffering.

646
00:45:06,940 --> 00:45:11,360
And if I'm honest,

647
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:14,720
the discouragement there,

648
00:45:14,720 --> 00:45:16,600
the voice that speaks into my life

649
00:45:16,600 --> 00:45:19,900
is not a voice that's telling me to cling to Jesus.

650
00:45:21,740 --> 00:45:23,480
And I know if that's my experience,

651
00:45:23,480 --> 00:45:24,960
that many of you are having that experience,

652
00:45:24,960 --> 00:45:25,920
that you are suffering

653
00:45:25,920 --> 00:45:29,180
and that what Jesus is telling you this morning

654
00:45:29,180 --> 00:45:30,240
is cling to me.

655
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:32,060
Hold on to me.

656
00:45:32,060 --> 00:45:33,360
Your suffering is temporary.

657
00:45:33,360 --> 00:45:34,540
It will go away.

658
00:45:34,540 --> 00:45:36,640
I have risen and am reigning

659
00:45:36,640 --> 00:45:38,540
and conquered all of the consequences

660
00:45:38,540 --> 00:45:40,420
of the sin that you're going through.

661
00:45:40,420 --> 00:45:42,960
But there's other voices

662
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:44,820
trying to get you to just numb out,

663
00:45:44,820 --> 00:45:47,400
to just forsake the Lord,

664
00:45:47,400 --> 00:45:48,800
to just get comfortable,

665
00:45:48,800 --> 00:45:50,920
to seek relief from your pain

666
00:45:50,920 --> 00:45:52,220
in any way, shape, or form.

667
00:45:52,220 --> 00:45:54,260
And the message that Jesus wants me to hear

668
00:45:54,260 --> 00:45:54,980
and you to hear

669
00:45:54,980 --> 00:45:56,120
and those of us that are suffering

670
00:45:56,120 --> 00:45:57,220
is hold on to me.

671
00:45:57,220 --> 00:46:03,580
Your suffering is temporary,

672
00:46:03,580 --> 00:46:05,440
but faithfulness to me

673
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:06,720
leads to eternal conquering.

674
00:46:06,720 --> 00:46:08,580
He who has ears, listen.

675
00:46:08,580 --> 00:46:11,260
This, I would argue,

676
00:46:11,260 --> 00:46:12,640
is the overarching point

677
00:46:12,640 --> 00:46:13,780
of Revelation 2 and 3.

678
00:46:13,780 --> 00:46:15,640
He who has ears, listen.

679
00:46:16,660 --> 00:46:18,860
Jesus is speaking to his church,

680
00:46:18,860 --> 00:46:20,240
but so is the enemy

681
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:20,940
through deception,

682
00:46:20,940 --> 00:46:22,260
distraction, discouragement.

683
00:46:22,260 --> 00:46:25,160
And there's a difference

684
00:46:25,160 --> 00:46:26,840
between hearing the voice of Jesus

685
00:46:26,840 --> 00:46:28,500
and listening to the voice of Jesus

686
00:46:28,500 --> 00:46:29,600
because if I'm honest right now,

687
00:46:29,600 --> 00:46:30,620
